        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Hiring individual creators works for occasional campaigns. It does not scale. When a brand needs 10&ndash;50+ videos per month across multiple products or accounts, the operational overhead of managing individual creator relationships becomes the bottleneck.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Why networks beat individual hiring</h3>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>Speed</strong> &mdash; a network can match creators to a brief within days. Individual hiring takes weeks of searching, outreach, and negotiation.</li>
          <li><strong>Variety</strong> &mdash; access to creators across demographics, styles, languages, and specialties. No single creator can cover all the angles a brand needs.</li>
          <li><strong>Redundancy</strong> &mdash; if one creator drops out or underperforms, the network provides replacements immediately. No single point of failure.</li>
          <li><strong>Quality control</strong> &mdash; the network reviews content before delivery. Brands receive production-ready videos, not raw footage that needs rounds of feedback.</li>
          <li><strong>Payment processing</strong> &mdash; one invoice to the network instead of managing individual payments to dozens of creators across different countries and payment methods.</li>
        </ul>

